{{- /*
  What each kind of machine manages. Paths are targets, relative to $HOME.

  Linux is the aether server, which only runs Pi and T3 Code, so it takes an allowlist: a file
  added for the laptop later stays off the server until it is listed here. Work never goes to
  aether (AWS and laptop-only configuration).
*/ -}}
{{ if eq .chezmoi.os "linux" -}}
**
!.chezmoiscripts
!.chezmoiscripts/*-linux-*.sh
!.config
!.config/git
!.config/git/**
!.config/mise
!.config/mise/**
!.config/systemd
!.config/systemd/**
!.config/fish
!.config/fish/config.fish
!.config/fish/themes
!.config/fish/themes/**
!.config/fish/functions
!.config/fish/functions/ai-sync.fish
!.config/fish/functions/pi.fish
!.config/fish/functions/__memini_namespace_prefix.fish
!.config/starship.toml
!.config/atuin
!.config/atuin/**
!.config/bat
!.config/bat/**
!.config/eza
!.config/eza/**
!.editorconfig
!.local
!.local/bin
!.local/bin/**
!.pi
!.pi/agent
# Keep the existing aether Pi runtime unchanged during the Mac-only rollout.
# These are the unaffected Pi resources; defaults, models, roles, prompts, routing
# and extensions are temporarily held back. Normal apply leaves ignored live files
# intact. Restore the broad Pi allowlist only with an approved server migration.
!.pi/agent/claude-bridge.json
!.pi/agent/claude
!.pi/agent/claude/**
!.pi/agent/agents
!.pi/agent/AGENTS.md
!.pi/shared
!.pi/shared/personal-policy.json
!.pi/shared/skills
!.pi/shared/skills/**
!.t3
!.t3/**
{{- else -}}
# Replaced on the Mac by extensions/profile/personal-gate.ts; aether's held runtime still uses it.
.pi/shared/personal-policy.json
.chezmoiscripts/*-linux-*.sh
.config/mise
.config/mise/**
.config/systemd
.config/systemd/**
.t3
.t3/**
{{- end }}
